    "notes": "Two New York sessions, 1961-11-13 (tracks 1, 2, 3, 7) and 1961-11-15 (tracks 4, 5, 6, 8); jazzdisco.org lists the matrix numbers by date (S3) and Wikipedia's track-to-date mapping agrees (S1). Studio: jazzdisco, Wikipedia and AllMusic all say New York City only, with no room named; one 2026 reissue marketing page (trackingangle.com) states the album was cut at Rudy Van Gelder's studio on November 19 and 21, 1961 — those dates contradict both the sessionography and Wikipedia, and a Discogs user note says the record was not an RVG date, so the venue is recorded as city-level only (S1, S3, S4). The tapes' 1961 session was produced by Bob Thiele (S1, S2); the LP's later companion Additions to Further Definitions (1966, Los Angeles) was produced by George Cates and is not part of this dossier. Engineer credited as 'Johnny Cue' on Wikipedia and 'John Cue' in AllMusic credits; AllMusic's combined credit table also lists Bobby Arnold and Jim Lockert as engineers, who belong to the 1966 Los Angeles dates (S1, S2). Carter's four-saxophone charts are the point of the record; the album is not a big-band date."
